  "caption": "Quinn's gym streak hit 84 days with no rest. Then warm-ups felt heavy and sleep slipped.\n\nTraining is the signal; much of the adaptation happens during repair. A deload is a planned lighter week, often five to seven days, to let that catch up.\n\nWhat often helps: reducing load and volume rather than stopping, timing a deload by how you're responding rather than the calendar (falling performance, heavy warm-ups, worse sleep, low motivation, morning stiffness, a run of small strains), and remembering strength largely holds through a lighter week. Travel or illness can count as an accidental deload.\n\nFatigue with weight loss, fevers, night sweats, breathlessness at rest or pain that wakes you needs a GP visit, not just a lighter week.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
